#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068491 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068717 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e107f878-5b22-54bf-90fc-b8ea8a22c77d" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Less Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/id #uuid "60c2e025-0b7e-5ac2-afec-adeb5f65eed1" :question/math-academy-id "e-14222" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\\left\\vert\\dfrac{x-1}{6}\\right\\vert \\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $\\dfrac{x-1}{6}$ whose distance from zero is less than or equal to $1.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq \\dfrac{x-1}{6} \\leq  1\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\frac{x-1}{6}\\le 1 \\\\ -6 & \\le x-1\\le 6 \\\\ -5 & \\le x\\le 7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068493 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/id #uuid "8497ea21-c194-5bbf-b501-a0e9749d8dc8" :question/math-academy-id "e-14227" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|12x - 5| > 7.$" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $12x - 5$ whose distance from zero is greater than $7.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-5 & <-7 & \\text{or} &  & 12x-5 & >7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-5 & <-7 &  &  & 12x-5 & >7 \\\\ 12x & <-2 &  &  & 12x & >12 \\\\ x & <-\\frac{2}{12} &  &  & x & >\\frac{12}{12} \\\\ x & <-\\frac{1}{6} &  &  & x & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & <-\\frac{1}{6} & \\text{or} &  & x & >1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068510 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"}] :question/id #uuid "12d8aea9-62dd-5181-bd6e-54c11eba4152" :question/math-academy-id "e-14708" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\\vert 10 - 2x \\vert +1 < 5$." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|10-2x|+1 & <5 \\\\ |10-2x| & <4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $10-2x$ whose distance from zero is less than $4.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-4 < 10 - 2x < 4\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4<10-2x & <4 \\\\ -14<-2x & <-6 \\\\ 14>2x & >6 \\\\ 7>x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the smaller number is on the left:\n\n$$\n3 < x < 7\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23f17c66-ee5f-5862-bbd9-df7e2337719f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -2\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510859} {:answer/id #uuid "43aad9b6-06b8-5090-a861-c22e239fefd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -4\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510934} {:answer/id #uuid "43ac02f0-bbf5-50c5-96dd-5aba08909745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -\\frac{3}{5}\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge -\\frac{1}{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510935} {:answer/id #uuid "44b0c010-8c4f-5f8b-9e9c-1cd9075b38eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le \\frac{5}{2}\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge 4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510938} {:answer/id #uuid "94a95ba2-27e3-51dd-94e1-78a5fe680a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le 1\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43ac02f0-bbf5-50c5-96dd-5aba08909745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -\\frac{3}{5}\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge -\\frac{1}{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510935} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8530bcb-8b8e-598a-ac17-38a2a589074a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f90e4de-4957-59b8-990a-09a9092a26e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-19350" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|5x+2|\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $5x+2$ whose distance from zero is greater than or equal to $1.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2 & \\le -1 & \\text{or} &  & 5x+2 & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2 & \\le -1 &  &  & 5x+2 & \\ge 1 \\\\ 5x & \\le -3 &  &  & 5x & \\ge -1 \\\\ x & \\le -\\frac{3}{5} &  &  & x & \\ge -\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & \\le -\\frac{3}{5} & \\text{or} &  & x & \\ge -\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068717 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e107f878-5b22-54bf-90fc-b8ea8a22c77d" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Less Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd4e8030-94fe-56aa-b5a3-23f94ae0c956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd4e8030-94fe-56aa-b5a3-23f94ae0c956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511304} :answer-field/id #uuid "48861394-50ec-54df-8b93-dcc5fd4bb869" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a23146c8-3400-5c70-8a31-ad8b237f9f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a23146c8-3400-5c70-8a31-ad8b237f9f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511122} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5a87638-c365-5e45-84cf-a39c2de661dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511419} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88d348bc-0475-5cca-be53-e26c51c508ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88d348bc-0475-5cca-be53-e26c51c508ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511066} :answer-field/id #uuid "fab47d47-48f0-502b-9d99-7f0d398eb9b2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dfe6edfc-d27b-50ff-aa28-a96fc85e1d12" :question/math-academy-id "q-212474" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|3x+2|<7.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x<$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $3x+2$ whose distance from zero is less than $7.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-7<3x+2<7\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7<3x+2 & <7 \\\\ -9<3x & <5 \\\\ -3<x & <\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068717 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e107f878-5b22-54bf-90fc-b8ea8a22c77d" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Less Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13817b1d-5fce-529d-8f9b-7b0617149423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510821} {:answer/id #uuid "36abe3a8-28f2-5cc2-9bad-e83391fce48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510904} {:answer/id #uuid "3d0dffa0-b169-5ae1-a016-418de2b2d5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510922} {:answer/id #uuid "8b02d4c3-cb7d-502b-979e-90622d4eb3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511069} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3f8dfc-bd30-57a3-8e58-10050f40289f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f3f8dfc-bd30-57a3-8e58-10050f40289f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511117} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8aa3d41-3265-55e2-8610-64e07f1b1be0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f658914c-7028-577a-9b28-3f8336734446" :question/math-academy-id "q-215469" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|\\frac{2x+1}{4}|-\\frac{3}{2}\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{2x+1}{4}|-\\frac{3}{2} & \\le 1 \\\\ |\\frac{2x+1}{4}| & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $\\frac{2x+1}{4}$ whose distance from zero is less than or equal to $\\frac{5}{2}.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\text{ }-\\frac{5}{2}\\le \\frac{2x+1}{4}\\le \\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2}\\le \\frac{2x+1}{4} & \\le \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -10\\le 2x+1 & \\le 10 \\\\ -11\\le 2x & \\le 9 \\\\ -\\frac{11}{2}\\le x & \\le \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0d1786b-ef7a-50ba-a2c1-15bd2b2e52bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0d1786b-ef7a-50ba-a2c1-15bd2b2e52bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511249} :answer-field/id #uuid "5abd1c81-55cb-5df8-b5f1-f81a16167daf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2615d33c-12ce-5201-84d1-8b5ec2754f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2615d33c-12ce-5201-84d1-8b5ec2754f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510864} :answer-field/id #uuid "894d5fc0-61ba-5e40-9d87-aa14a2b88f4d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511383} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "240db0bb-0455-5f41-a0df-c1e8f1a12e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "240db0bb-0455-5f41-a0df-c1e8f1a12e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510860} :answer-field/id #uuid "99213336-50fc-5fea-97c9-bdf16997d0ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8ba584f9-4667-5d0f-bd62-9fcff937c1e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-215488" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\\frac{3}{5}+|\\frac{1-3x}{5}|<2.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}+|\\frac{1-3x}{5}| & <2 \\\\ |\\frac{1-3x}{5}| & <\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $\\frac{1-3x}{5}$ whose distance from zero is less than $\\frac{7}{5}.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{7}{5}<\\frac{1-3x}{5}<\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{5}<\\frac{1-3x}{5} & <\\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -7<1-3x & <7 \\\\ -8<-3x & <6 \\\\ 8>3x & >-6 \\\\ \\frac{8}{3}>x & >-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the smaller number is on the left:\n\n$$\n-2<x<\\frac{8}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c429898a-21b3-561e-94f6-8ff522fbd96c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c429898a-21b3-561e-94f6-8ff522fbd96c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511186} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab4ce6ab-f572-536f-b69b-26107e70c78f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e030f78-1887-5b4f-91f6-e9f93a8adee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e030f78-1887-5b4f-91f6-e9f93a8adee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510950} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0a61e3-aadd-51f2-af52-df568c7fa6e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f3530a-e641-5d6c-b5f8-7527ed951265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16f3530a-e641-5d6c-b5f8-7527ed951265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510833} :answer-field/id #uuid "48a7fd8b-fc8e-504d-805e-8ece07aca323" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0ceea8c0-f989-54a6-9f70-92e530683a94" :question/math-academy-id "q-215489" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $1+|17-3h|\\le 9.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$h\\le $\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+|17-3h| & \\le 9 \\\\ |17-3h| & \\le 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $17-3h$ whose distance from zero is less than or equal to $8.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-8\\le 17-3h\\le 8\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8\\le 17-3h & \\le 8 \\\\ -25\\le -3h & \\le -9 \\\\ 25\\ge 3h & \\ge 9 \\\\ \\frac{25}{3}\\ge h & \\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the smaller number is on the left:\n\n$$\n3\\le h\\le \\frac{25}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88027a38-f810-5e63-aba9-d53d0556696f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88027a38-f810-5e63-aba9-d53d0556696f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511063} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcca67ee-d00b-5ed9-a1a5-a17cc2e60ae9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38782a03-b1f9-5e6d-8e0e-795314ea535c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38782a03-b1f9-5e6d-8e0e-795314ea535c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510910} :answer-field/id #uuid "33b677ae-2eee-5574-a670-188edbba3875" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56ae4ec4-c928-5d91-9771-f55187807779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56ae4ec4-c928-5d91-9771-f55187807779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510967} :answer-field/id #uuid "503e8508-9d51-5534-9ba4-e03eddaf3997" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a92a4124-bc7c-5436-968f-ce759fb4d648" :question/math-academy-id "q-215707" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|\\frac{5-9a}{2}|\\ge 7.$\n\n$a$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$\\,$ or $\\,a\\ge $\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $\\frac{5-9a}{2}$ whose distance from zero is greater than or equal to $7.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-9a}{2} & \\le -7 & \\text{or} &  & \\frac{5-9a}{2} & \\ge 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-9a}{2} & \\le -7 &  &  & \\frac{5-9a}{2} & \\ge 7 \\\\ 5-9a & \\le -14 &  &  & 5-9a & \\ge 14 \\\\ -9a & \\le -19 &  &  & -9a & \\ge 9 \\\\ 9a & \\ge 19 &  &  & 9a & \\le -9 \\\\ a & \\ge \\frac{19}{9} &  &  & a & \\le -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & \\le -1 & \\text{or} &  & a & \\ge \\frac{19}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22bca241-56fc-57ff-91be-5e58e2055c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6<z<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510856} {:answer/id #uuid "67885a2b-3782-5eff-9553-a065c134d72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<-2\\,$ or $\\,z>1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511001} {:answer/id #uuid "79fd5220-180b-5a65-9715-68413d928a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<-2\\,$ or $\\,z>4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511034} {:answer/id #uuid "a14a9c3c-aba8-5d6f-a2ba-dea60b34d636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<z<1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511120} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e7ca7d-647e-5b45-8cc4-20f7f026eba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<1\\,$ or $\\,z>6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67885a2b-3782-5eff-9553-a065c134d72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<-2\\,$ or $\\,z>1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511001} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdeb6dc8-1ec1-52bb-af0d-d8dc93ce7c2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e891fb42-cafd-57b7-9773-6b5a4bb29926" :question/math-academy-id "q-29942" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|4z+2|>6.$" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $4z+2$ whose distance from zero is greater than $6.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4z+2 & <-6 & \\text{or} &  & 4z+2 & >6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4z+2 & <-6 &  &  & 4z+2 & >6 \\\\ 4z & <-8 &  &  & 4z & >4 \\\\ z & <-2 &  &  & z & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & <-2 & \\text{or} &  & z & >1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0213c4e3-50ba-556f-ba2d-7eab3e633c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<3\\,$ or $\\,z>5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510778} {:answer/id #uuid "5099b5f9-89a1-57ab-b422-907c29d9b8cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<-2\\,$ or $\\,z>2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510955} {:answer/id #uuid "648b105b-a272-5e72-89b9-c740ccf253ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<-4\\,$ or $\\,z>-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510995} {:answer/id #uuid "953d6fbb-c6b7-5205-9208-c5a86b5d1c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<4$ or $z>8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511090} {:answer/id #uuid "dea0ca30-4acf-5241-b898-f1f35edf8ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<-8\\,$ or $\\,z>2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0213c4e3-50ba-556f-ba2d-7eab3e633c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z<3\\,$ or $\\,z>5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510778} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0ed7d8-cbd1-55a5-898d-36649e01d3f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a81effc-bede-5f14-bdb7-3f40c0a9e067" :question/math-academy-id "q-29943" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|8-2z|>2.$" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $8-2z$ whose distance from zero is greater than $2.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-2z & <-2 & \\text{or} &  & 8-2z & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-2z & <-2 &  &  & 8-2z & >2 \\\\ -2z & <-10 &  &  & -2z & >-6 \\\\ z & >5 &  &  & z & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z<3 &  & \\text{or} &  & z>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
